---
// src/pages/about.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ButtonLink from '../components/ui/ButtonLink.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Learn about Mohammad Azharuddin — Senior Software Engineer, Integration & Observability specialist, and Pega CSSA since December 2012."
>
  <div class="container-content py-20 sm:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-article">
      <!-- Eyebrow + heading -->
      <p class="text-eyebrow mb-4">About me</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-text tracking-tight mb-8 text-balance">
        Mohammad Azharuddin
      </h1>

      <!-- Introduction -->
      <div class="prose text-muted leading-relaxed space-y-6 mb-12">
        <p class="text-text text-lg">
          I'm a Senior Software Engineer and Certified Pega Senior System Architect (CSSA) based in Hyderabad,
          India. With continuous enterprise IT experience since December 2012, I specialize in enterprise
          integration architectures, observability pipelines (Splunk), Python backend microservices,
          and workflow automation.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text">Career Background</h2>
        <p>
          My engineering journey began with an Electronics & Communication Engineering degree from
          Osmania University (MJ College of Engineering and Technology) in 2012. I started my career in December 2012
          at <strong>Wipro Technologies</strong>, where I ranked first in my training batch of 40+ peers
          and earned a Certificate of Recognition for rapid proof-of-concept development in Python, web applications, and Linux systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2015, I joined <strong>Astreya supporting the Google India account</strong>, spending over six years
          architecting Pega workflows, secure Google Drive API attachment integrations, and developing an internal
          tooling suite of browser extensions, automated CSAT pipelines with BigQuery, and operational chatbots.
        </p>
        <p>
          At <strong>Cognizant</strong> (since March 2022), I focus on enterprise integration, observability, and workflow architecture across tier-1 client assignments:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 pl-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Cisco Splunk (December 2025 – Present):</strong> Engineering enterprise observability pipelines, log analytics, Technology Add-ons (TAs), and optimized SPL query monitoring across distributed systems.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Verizon (June 2024 – November 2025):</strong> Served as Pega Lead, architecting 5G Fixed Wireless Access (FWA) customer onboarding, enforcing Pega 8.8.3 guardrails, and improving SLA compliance from 92% to 98%.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google India Account (March 2022 – June 2024):</strong> Delivered critical case management workflows, Google Drive API secure attachment offloading, and automated Python microservices.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text">Hands-On Technical Exploration & aforapple.fun</h2>
        <p>
          I strongly believe that hands-on exploration beyond daily enterprise tooling keeps an engineer sharp and adaptable.
          As a personal engineering project, I created <a href="https://aforapple.fun" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent underline hover:text-accent-hover">aforapple.fun</a>,
          an interactive educational web application designed for early childhood learners and classroom smart TVs. Building it end-to-end — from HTML5 canvas tracing logic and Smart TV D-pad remote navigation to lightweight serverless APIs and Android packaging — offered valuable hands-on experience in building accessible, low-latency client experiences.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text">Engineering Principles</h2>
        <ul class="list-none p-0 space-y-3">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-accent font-bold mt-0.5">01.</span>
            <span><strong>Understand the problem before touching code:</strong> The best software is often the simplest workflow that eliminates operational friction.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-accent font-bold mt-0.5">02.</span>
            <span><strong>Guardrails & maintainability matter:</strong> Whether in Pega PRPC or Python microservices, adhering to strict design guardrails saves months of migration pain later.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-accent font-bold mt-0.5">03.</span>
            <span><strong>Automate the mundane:</strong> Repetitive human steps are opportunities to build clean scripts, browser extensions, or queue processors.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text">Technical Exploration</h2>
        <p>
          I am an early and active adopter of Agentic AI coding workflows (Claude Code, OpenAI Codex) to accelerate
          architectural reviews, test automation, and system refactoring. I hold CSSA and CSA certifications, and am currently
          preparing for the <strong>Pega Lead System Architect (LSA)</strong> certification.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- CTAs -->
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-8 border-t border-border">
        <ButtonLink href="/experience" variant="primary" size="md">
          View full experience
        </ButtonLink>
        <ButtonLink href={site.resumePath} variant="secondary" size="md" external>
          Download resume (PDF)
        </ButtonLink>
        <ButtonLink href="/contact" variant="ghost" size="md">
          Get in touch
        </ButtonLink>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
